17:T630,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"When is the Commonwealth Scholarship 2027 deadline?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The published central deadline for the listed 2027–2028 Master’s and PhD schemes was 20 October 2026 at 16:00 BST and has passed. Check the official portal for any amendment. A later nomination or university task does not itself reopen the CSC application."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I apply directly to the CSC without a nominator?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The current scheme requires an application through the stated CSC system and an approved nominating body. A central form alone does not replace nomination."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Pakistan eligible for Commonwealth Master's Scholarships?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Pakistan is on the current eligible-country list for the Master's route. All personal eligibility and nominator requirements still apply."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is the Commonwealth Scholarship fully funded?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The official scheme describes tuition, travel, living support and other applicable allowances. Read the exact current benefits and conditions for your route and circumstances."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I need university admission separately?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Follow the current CSC and nominator instructions for course choices and admission. Scholarship nomination does not remove university academic requirements."}}]}1:["$","main",null,{"id":"main-content","className":"editorial-page editorial-page--guide","children":[[["$","script","0",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"@id\":\"https://aspirecompass.org/scholarships/commonwealth/\",\"name\":\"Commonwealth Scholarships 2027–2028 application guide\",\"description\":\"The published 